[7.999676, "i", "printf '%s\\n' '===== USTAR.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/USTAR.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== DESK.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/DESK.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== APPLY.txt ====='; cat /app/yarnwell/APPLY.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== SEAL.txt ====='; cat /app/cordpit/SEAL.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== TREE.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/TREE.txt\n"]
[8.000887, "o", "printf '%s\\n' '===== USTAR.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/USTAR.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== DESK.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/DESK.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== APPLY.txt ====='; cat /app/yarnwell/APPLY.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== SEAL.txt ====='; cat /app/cordpit/SEAL.txt; printf '%s\\n' '===== TREE.txt ====='; cat /app/treenotes/TREE.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[8.001101, "o", "===== USTAR.txt =====\r\n"]
[8.002773, "o", "ustar member header is 512 bytes. name occupies bytes 0-99. size octal occupies 124-135 (the slice end is 136). typeflag sits at 156: regular file uses ASCII 0 (the byte that Python writes as b\"0\"). Payload follows the header and is padded to 512.\r\n\r\nwalk_sig is hashlib.sha256 hex of regular-file names joined by newline in apply order (SHA-256). Length is 64. Alphabet is 0123456789abcdef.\r\n\r\nA quarry of truncated bytes or a non-ustar stream such as not-an-archive returns nonzero. A ledger filled with xxxx is junk and quarry must rebuild members.idx from the sealed kith.\r\n\r\npython3 -c import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(sys.stdin.buffer.read()).hexdigest())\r\n"]
[8.003321, "o", "===== DESK.txt =====\r\n"]
[8.00477, "o", "Desk JSON keys: timezone, cluster, log_events, member_count, source_kith, walk_sig.\r\n\r\nsys.conf uses key=value lines. timezone and cluster come from the sys.conf payload the mill applies. log_events is the lexicographically sorted unique event strings from every app.log payload. member_count is the integer of regular-file payloads applied. source_kith is the archive basename.\r\n\r\nA brief archive copied to /tmp/kestrel.kith sits outside /app/sealwell. The sealed original also lives at /app/seed/sealwell/kestrel.kith.\r\n"]
[8.006046, "o", "===== APPLY.txt =====\r\n"]
[8.007205, "o", "operator note: APPLY\r\n"]
[8.007418, "o", "===== SEAL.txt =====\r\n"]
[8.008506, "o", "cordpit notes: two brief processes on one sealed kith must parse to one object. Paths outside sealwell fail.\r\n"]
[8.008731, "o", "===== TREE.txt =====\r\n"]
[8.009693, "o", "idxmill\r\noverlaypit\r\nlogbag\r\nsiltcli\r\nustarwalk\r\ncfgbag\r\noffseturn\r\npaxcue\r\npidhash\r\nkeeppit\r\n"]
